Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

*(You can also use the constructor / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync`.)*

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this class finish
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly (before any / after all tests)

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start WireMock
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stop WireMock
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once per entire test session (global start / end)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // EF Core migrations, spin up container, etc.
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // drop database / stop container
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After | Method must be |
|-------|--------|-------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | instance |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | **static** |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** |

**Global hooks:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (or `Class`/`Assembly` variants) to run cross-cutting logic for *every* test/class across the entire run (e.g., logging, timing). These can live in any class.

All hooks optionally accept a context parameter and/or a `CancellationToken`.
